<title>INDONESIA: Bimantara 1996 net up to 157.51 bln rph.</title>
<headline>Bimantara 1996 net up to 157.51 bln rph.</headline>
<dateline>JAKARTA 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Twelve months to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>		(in billion rupiah unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			   157.51 vs 117.78</p>
<p>    Earnings per share (rupiah)	155  vs 134</p>
<p>Non financial services and classified financial services</p>
<p>    Revenues			     847.38 vs 702.18</p>
<p>    Gross profit			 373.59 vs 308.84</p>
<p>    Operating profit		   211.86 vs 173.44</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit		     236.24 vs 189.62</p>
<p>Unclassified financial services</p>
<p>    Revenues			     43.07  vs 33.61</p>
<p>    Expenses			     38.45  vs 30.46</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit		     4.62   vs  3.15</p>
<p>Consolidated earnings</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit		     240.86 vs 192.77</p>
<p>Profit before minority interest 190.31 vs 151.72</p>
<p>    Retained earnings		   302.34 vs 162.66</p>
<p>NOTE: The results were audited. PT Bimantara Citra is one of Indonesia's largest business groups, with interests ranging from telecommunications, vehicle assembly, financial services to property.</p>
<p>-- Jakarta newsroom +6221 384-6364</p>
</text>
